# wowzaV9-Pro
# ============
# This repo is a REBUILD, not a fork.
#
# The folder it lives in was previously v10 (v9's staging sandbox) and still holds a stale
# copy of v9 at commit 12a3dc8 on disk. Prompt 2 section 3 says never delete those research
# assets, so they stay exactly where they are — but they are NOT committed here. Code is
# ported into src/ deliberately, module by module, each with an OLD / NEW / WHY / RISK note.
# Inheriting a stale clone wholesale would reintroduce bugs v9 has since fixed.
#
# Strategy: ignore every root entry, then re-admit only the Pro tree.

/*

!/.gitignore
!/.github/
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/config/
!/src/
!/registry/
!/experiments/
!/tests/
!/data/
!/models/
!/output/

# ── Secrets: never, by any path ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# v10's .env carries live API-Football, Google and GitHub credentials. They must reach CI as
# repository secrets, never as a committed file.
.env
.env.*
.api_keys
**/secrets.toml
**/bot_config.json
*.pem
*.key

# ── Large or regenerable data ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Pro season store is built by importers from v9's committed output (the pattern v11
# already uses: read the baseline's public data over HTTP). Committing 187MB of legacy
# parquet and backtest CSVs would tax every clone forever for data we can rebuild.
*.parquet
*.xlsx
*.zip
data/**
models/**
output/**

# ...but keep the empty scaffolding and the small machine-readable truth files.
!data/.gitkeep
!models/.gitkeep
!output/.gitkeep
!output/system_registry.json
!output/pro_readiness.json
!output/collect_health.json
# Combo research artifacts. Named INDIVIDUALLY rather than with an output/combo*.csv glob: a
# glob here is a repo-wide rule whose blast radius is every file anyone adds later matching it,
# and this file's whole design is deny-all plus a short explicit allowlist. These three are the
# durable measured evidence the bet-builder work rests on -- dependency ratios over 23,604
# fixtures and 67,052 player-matches -- and they are small (310 KB, 4 KB, 19 KB).
#
# bet_builder_candidates.csv is DELIBERATELY NOT allowlisted: it is 1.7 MB, regenerated on every
# run from these inputs plus current fixtures, and it would churn the repo daily for no
# evidential gain. The matrices are the finding; the candidates are a rendering of it.
!output/combo_dependency_matrix.csv
!output/combo_dependency_stability.csv
!output/player_combo_dependency.csv
# The two above were deliberately excluded while nothing read them. v9's dashboard now does
# (pages/14), and it reads Pro's committed output over a sibling checkout — an ignored file
# there is not "not shown yet", it is a page that renders empty and reads as "no combos
# today". The settled record is also the results history the dashboard tracks won/lost from,
# so it has to accumulate in git the same way the weekly audit record does.
# Named file by file, never a glob: `git add` on an ignored path aborts the WHOLE add and
# stages nothing, which is how two earlier commits silently saved no matrices at all.
!output/bet_builder_settled.csv
!output/bet_builder_candidates.csv
# The notify dedup state. It MUST persist between runs or every run re-sends the whole board as
# NEW — the same failure shape as v9's duplicate-tip flood.
!output/combo_notified.json
# The forward 1X2 paper record. MUST be committed or the whole point is lost: it is evidence of
# what was believed BEFORE kickoff, and a record that does not survive the run that wrote it
# proves nothing. Small and append-only — one row per fixture the model could price.
!output/paper_1x2.csv
# The trained 1X2 parameters the paper logger predicts from. Committed so a CI run scores from
# the SAME model a human evaluated, rather than silently refitting on whatever data it happens
# to find.
!output/model_1x2.json
!output/model_1x2_eval.csv
# The weekly audit record. Committed so the history of "was the pipeline persisting" is itself
# persisted — a check whose result is thrown away cannot show a slow decline.
!output/weekly_audit.json
!output/snapshot_coverage.json
!output/clv_enriched.csv
# The monthly out-of-sample evaluation record. Committed for the same reason: a hypothesis test
# whose result is discarded cannot show whether an effect held up over time.
!output/monthly_eval.json
# Cross-model correlation study. Committed for that same reason and one more: its whole value is
# the TREND. "ou25_standard does better when btts agrees" is a pre-registration candidate at
# n_both=33 and nothing else; the only thing that can promote or kill it is the same table
# recomputed as n grows. A run whose result is discarded can never do that, and would instead
# invite re-reading the best of thirty comparisons as a fresh discovery every time. Small: one
# row per ordered model pair.
!output/cross_model_correlation.csv
# Calibration study. Committed because the SHAPE of the miss is the finding and it should be
# re-checked as n grows: the model is UNDER-confident overall but OVER-confident in the high
# bins where it actually bets, and that split is what a single average hides.
!output/calibration_study.csv
!output/calibration_bins.csv
# Per-league threshold curves and their out-of-sample verdicts. Committed because the whole
# point is to re-run it as cells grow: today 0 of 23 survive, and the record of WHEN that
# changes is the only thing that can ever justify moving a live threshold.
!output/threshold_verdicts.csv
!output/threshold_curves.csv
# THE learning-health record. Committed because the question is historical: 'when did the
# models last actually learn' cannot be answered by a file that only holds the current
# run, and every failure this estate has had ran for WEEKS before anyone noticed.
!output/ml_learning_health.json
# The mixed/stacked challenger evaluation. Committed because its answer is expected to
# CHANGE: model_snapshots only began in August, so today's test window is ~8 days. The
# verdict that matters is the one taken when the window is a season long.
!output/mixed_model_eval.json
# Pure hit-rate study. Kept as its own artifact and NOT merged into any other research
# output: it deliberately ignores odds, edge, CLV and ROI, and mixing it with an
# edge-based table is exactly how someone later reads a 76% hit rate as 76% profitable.
!output/pick_accuracy.json
# Accuracy-vs-edge and the combo test. Committed because its central number — the price a
# book must offer for the Over2.5+BTTS double to break even — is the thing to re-check
# as more real prices accumulate.
!output/accuracy_vs_edge.json
# Accumulator study across SEPARATE fixtures. The number to re-check is leg EV: above 1.0
# an acca compounds upward, below it compounds downward, and nothing else matters.
!output/accumulators.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PURE PREDICTION RESEARCH LAB (src/prediction_lab).
#
# Named file by file rather than with an `output/pure_prediction/*` glob, for the reason the
# combo block above gives: a glob would also sweep in the two working artifacts this lab writes
# and must NOT commit --
#   feature_matrix.parquet   23 MB, rebuilt from v9's history in seconds, pure cache
#   oof_probabilities.parquet / scoreline_oof.parquet   per-fixture predictions, regenerable
# Committing those would add ~30 MB per weekly run to a repo that has to stay clonable in CI.
!output/pure_prediction/
!output/pure_prediction/data_inventory.csv
!output/pure_prediction/leakage_perturbation.csv
!output/pure_prediction/leakage_single_feature_auc.csv
!output/pure_prediction/target_performance.csv
!output/pure_prediction/model_comparison.csv
!output/pure_prediction/feature_ablation.csv
!output/pure_prediction/time_ablation.csv
!output/pure_prediction/market_ablation.csv
!output/pure_prediction/league_performance.csv
!output/pure_prediction/learning_curves.csv
!output/pure_prediction/chronological_folds.csv
!output/pure_prediction/confidence_calibration.csv
!output/pure_prediction/confidence_topk.csv
!output/pure_prediction/goal_distribution_comparison.csv
!output/pure_prediction/consistency_violations.csv
!output/pure_prediction/player_goalscorer_performance.csv
!output/pure_prediction/player_match_interactions.csv
!output/pure_prediction/player_v9_column_check.csv
!output/pure_prediction/cross_market_matrix.csv
!output/pure_prediction/conditional_outcomes.csv
!output/pure_prediction/stratified_control.csv
!output/pure_prediction/agreement_analysis.csv
!output/pure_prediction/disagreement_analysis.csv
!output/pure_prediction/prediction_correlation.csv
!output/pure_prediction/error_correlation.csv
!output/pure_prediction/meta_model_comparison.csv
!output/pure_prediction/cross_market_lr_tests.csv
!output/pure_prediction/cross_market_discoveries.csv
!output/pure_prediction/cross_market_manifest.json
!output/pure_prediction/research_manifest.json
!output/pure_prediction/verdicts.json
!output/pure_prediction/verdicts.txt
!output/pure_prediction/cross_market_verdicts.json
!output/pure_prediction/cross_market_verdicts.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ARCHITECTURE AUDIT (src/architecture). Named file by file, same reason as the blocks above.
# canonical_match_history.parquet is DERIVED and rebuildable from raw in a couple of minutes, so
# it is deliberately NOT committed -- it would add several MB per run to a repo CI has to clone,
# and committing a derived table invites someone to edit it instead of the builder.
!output/architecture/
!output/architecture/data_lineage.csv
!output/architecture/training_data_health.json
!output/architecture/player_gap.json
!output/architecture/entity_resolution_audit.csv
!output/architecture/canonical_match_manifest.json
!output/architecture/training_dataset_comparison.csv
!output/architecture/training_dataset_bootstrap.csv
!output/architecture/v9_training_probe.json
!output/architecture/architecture_verdict.json
!output/architecture/architecture_verdict.txt
!output/architecture/workflow_lineage.csv
!output/architecture/workflow_write_overlap.csv
!output/architecture/canonical_player_manifest.json
!output/architecture/canonical_market_manifest.json
!output/architecture/canonical_match_training_manifest.json
!output/architecture/canonical_player_training_manifest.json
!output/architecture/training_flow_canary.json
!output/architecture/asof_coverage.csv
!output/architecture/asof_manifest.json
!output/architecture/fixture_resolution_manifest.json
# The provider lookup result IS committed, unlike the other parquets: 709 rows, it is an
# immutable fact about finished fixtures, and committing it means CI never re-spends the calls.
!output/architecture/fixture_id_map.parquet

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SHADOW LEARNING (src/shadow_learning). Named file by file; the parquet universes and the
# walk-forward prediction ledger are derived and stay out.
!output/shadow_learning/
!output/shadow_learning/dataset_inventory.csv
!output/shadow_learning/dataset_quality_tiers.csv
!output/shadow_learning/incremental_fixture_inventory.csv
!output/shadow_learning/incremental_by_league.csv
!output/shadow_learning/distribution_shift.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_core.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_core_bootstrap.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_window.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_window_bootstrap.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_recency.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_recency_bootstrap.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_dupes.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_dupes_bootstrap.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_covid.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_covid_bootstrap.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_completeness.csv
!output/shadow_learning/experiment_completeness_bootstrap.csv
!output/shadow_learning/monthly_walkforward_performance.csv
!output/shadow_learning/walkforward_trends.csv
!output/shadow_learning/retrain_gate_backtest.csv
!output/shadow_learning/league_target_comparison.csv
!output/shadow_learning/season_phase.csv
!output/shadow_learning/model_age.csv
!output/shadow_learning/learning_scorecard.csv
# Scheduler observability (Prompt 01 section 7). Committed because the QUESTION is historical:
# "is the observed cadence degrading" cannot be answered by a file that only ever holds the
# current run. Both are small — one JSON object each, no per-row data.
!output/scheduler_health.json
!output/high_activity_coverage.json
# Per-table import accounting for the builder evidence: rows seen, imported, skipped as
# duplicates, canonical total. Committed because "the importer ran" and "the importer stored
# anything" are different claims, and only the second one is worth alarming on.
!output/combo_import_health.json
!output/output_manifest.json

# The season store IS the deliverable and must survive across CI runs, so it is committed.
# Safe to commit because writes are run-partitioned (one small file per table per run) and
# the append-only histories are watermarked — a repeat run adds nothing.
!data/season_*/
!data/season_*/**
# Watermarks must persist or every run re-imports v9's full odds history (~40k rows).
!output/import_watermarks.json

# The git-history extract (935 fixtures). Committed so the results fetch can run in CI WITHOUT
# cloning v9's 1.3GB history: the extract needs all 702 predictions.csv commits, the results
# fetch needs none of them. Also means the expensive walk is done once, not per run.
!data/_backfill_fixtures.parquet

# The JOINED result — and the gate for pro_backfill_results.yml, which skips when this exists.
# MUST be committed or the gate can never see it and the hourly schedule would redo the whole
# fetch forever. Caught before shipping: `data/**` above would otherwise have ignored it.
!data/_backfill_joined.parquet
# The resolver version that produced the join above. MUST be committed alongside it: the workflow
# gate compares this to RESOLVER_VERSION in the source to decide whether an improvement to
# club-name resolution needs re-applying. Ignored, it would read as version 0 forever and the job
# would redo the whole fetch on every schedule.
!data/_backfill_resolver_version
!registry/**
!experiments/**/manifest.json
!experiments/**/metrics.json
!experiments/**/by_league.csv
!experiments/**/calibration.csv

# ── Caches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
**/*_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
# API-Football /fixtures/statistics response cache. Regenerable, and ~24,500 JSON files.
cache/af_stats/
!output/news_impact.json
!output/clv_enriched.csv
